skills/dev/SKILL.md changed (design.md -> plan.md) but the two GIT-TRACKED agent
mirrors (.codex/skills, .agents/skills — the packaging/Codex staging dirs) were not
regenerated, tripping the skills-sync drift gate. Regenerated via populateAgentSkills
(only:dev); drift test now passes.
---
 .agents/skills/dev/SKILL.md | 2 +-
 .codex/skills/dev/SKILL.md  | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.agents/skills/dev/SKILL.md b/.agents/skills/dev/SKILL.md
index 5b58ec65..412fa519 100644
--- a/.agents/skills/dev/SKILL.md
+++ b/.agents/skills/dev/SKILL.md
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 name: dev
 description: >
   Forge DEV stage — implement an already-planned /plan task list into committed, test-backed
-  code. Reads tasks.md + design.md, then drives each task through a subagent TDD loop
+  code. Reads tasks.md + plan.md, then drives each task through a subagent TDD loop
   (implementer → spec-compliance reviewer → code-quality reviewer) with RED-GREEN-REFACTOR,
   HARD-GATE evidence checks, and a spec-gap decision score. Use when a plan and task list
   already exist and it is time to implement — triggers: "/dev", "start the dev stage", "build
diff --git a/.codex/skills/dev/SKILL.md b/.codex/skills/dev/SKILL.md
